  <h2>Derived Data</h2>
  <div class="base__accordions testing-data" data-level="1">
                                                                    <div class="accordion-item level-1">
          <h3 class="accordion-title" aria-label="Press enter to open" tabindex="0">Soot Yield</h3>
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <p>Soot yield [g/g] was calculated from smoke obscuration data collected in cone calorimeter experiments conducted at heat fluxes of 25 kW/m<sup>2</sup>, 50 kW/m<sup>2</sup>, and 75 kW/m<sup>2</sup>.</p>
                                                                      <div class="responsive-table"><table class="dataframe">
  <thead>
    <tr style="text-align: right;">
      <th>Incident Heat Flux [kW/m²]</th>
      <th>Mean Soot Yield [g/g]</th>
      <th>Soot Yield Std. Dev. [g/g]</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>25</td>
      <td>0.013</td>
      <td>0.002</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>50</td>
      <td>0.013</td>
      <td>0.0</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>75</td>
      <td>0.015</td>
      <td>0.0</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
                                    </div>
        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item level-1">
          <h3 class="accordion-title" aria-label="Press enter to open" tabindex="0">Effective Heat of Combustion (&#916;h<sub>c</sub>)</h3>
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <p>Effective heat of combustion [MJ/kg] is calculated from data collected in micro-scale combustion calorimeter experiments.</p>
                          <div class="base__accordions testing-data" data-level="2">
                                  <div class="accordion-item level-2">
                    <h3 class="accordion-title" aria-label="Press enter to open" tabindex="0">Micro-scale Combustion Calorimeter</h3>
                    <div class="accordion-body">
                                                                    <div class="responsive-table"><table class="dataframe">
  <thead>
    <tr style="text-align: right;">
      <th>Value</th>
      <th>R1</th>
      <th>R2</th>
      <th>R3</th>
      <th>Mean</th>
      <th>Std. Dev.</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Heat of Combustion (MJ/kg)</td>
      <td>25.4</td>
      <td>25.15</td>
      <td>25.7</td>
      <td>25.42</td>
      <td>0.22</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
                                          </div>
                  </div>
                              </div>
                      </div>
        </div>
                        <div class="accordion-item level-1">
          <h3 class="accordion-title" aria-label="Press enter to open" tabindex="0">Temperature at Onset of Decomposition</h3>
          <div class="accordion-body">
            <p>The temperature at onset of decomposition [T<sub>onset</sub>] is a derived quantity computed from data collected in simultaneous thermal analyzer experiments.</p>
                                                                      <div class="responsive-table"><table class="dataframe">
  <thead>
    <tr style="text-align: right;">
      <th></th>
      <th>3 &deg;C/min</th>
      <th>10 &deg;C/min</th>
      <th>30 &deg;C/min</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th>Mean Onset Temperature (&deg;C)</th>
      <td>239</td>
      <td>252</td>
      <td>281</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Std. Dev. Onset Temperature (&deg;C)</th>
      <td>4</td>
      <td>1</td>
      <td>4</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Mean Normalized MLR at Onset (1/s)</th>
      <td>1.05e-03</td>
      <td>1.00e-03</td>
      <td>1.26e-03</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Std. Dev. Normalized MLR at Onset (1/s)</th>
      <td>0.15e-03</td>
      <td>0.09e-03</td>
      <td>0.05e-03</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Mean Mass Fraction at Onset</th>
      <td>0.98</td>
      <td>0.98</td>
      <td>0.98</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Std. Dev. Mass Fraction at Onset</th>
      <td>0.00</td>
      <td>0.00</td>
      <td>0.00</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Mean Temperature at end of Decomposition (&deg;C)</th>
      <td>398</td>
      <td>414</td>
      <td>441</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Std. Dev. Temperature at end of Decomposition (&deg;C)</th>
      <td>0</td>
      <td>1</td>
      <td>1</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
